## 📊 Simulation Results

### Original 30-Trial Experiment

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `S4_full_results.json` | E[ATC], VaR₉₀, CE, Friedman ranks — IEEE 30-bus and 118-bus |
| `S6_nrpg246_results.json` | E[ATC], VaR₉₀ — NRPG 246-bus (30 trials) |
| `S2_baseline_results.json` | Deterministic ATC baseline (5 trials) |

### Major Revision Validation Results

| File | Manuscript Table | Key Finding |
|------|-----------------|-------------|
| `S07_data02_dnn_validation_summary.csv` | Tab. I | R²=0.9975/0.9675/0.9999 |
| `S08_data02_oos_summary.csv` | Tab. VIII | Max OOS bias = +2.06% |
| `S09_data02_carbon_sensitivity.csv` | Tab. IX | Binding at 120% budget |
| `S10_data02_n1_summary.csv` | — | MAE ratio N-1/normal = 1.2× |
| `S11_data02_model_comparison.csv` | Tab. II | DNN beats RF/LR by 41-48% MAE |

---

## 🗺️ NRPG 246-Bus Network

The `NRPG246_full.json` file contains a pandapower-compatible network
object for the Northern Regional Power Grid of India:

- 246 buses · 612 branches · 42 generators · 19,994.8 MW load
- Monitored corridor: **Chamera–Jalandhar 400 kV** (bus 3 → bus 73)

> **Data attribution:** The original NRPG 246-bus data was sourced from
> the Power Systems Laboratory, IIT Kanpur, where it was publicly available
> during the period of this research. Researchers requiring the original
> MATPOWER case file should contact IIT Kanpur directly.
> The `NRPG246_full.json` is a pandapower derivative for academic use only.

---

## 🔬 Results at a Glance

### DNN Surrogate vs Baseline Models (IEEE 118-bus)

| Model | R² | RMSE (PU) | MAE (PU) |
|-------|-----|-----------|---------|
| Linear Regression | 0.9096 | 0.0611 | 0.0406 |
| Random Forest | 0.9005 | 0.0641 | 0.0458 |
| **DNN (ours)** | **0.9675** | **0.0367** | **0.0239** |

### Out-of-Sample Validation (500 independent scenarios)

| System | Max OOS Bias | VaR₉₀ Generalises |
|--------|-------------|------------------|
| IEEE 30-bus | +1.40% (BBO) | ✅ Yes |
| IEEE 118-bus | +2.06% (GWO) | ✅ Yes |
| NRPG 246-bus | +0.004% (CSHO) | ✅ Yes |

